      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, dang, I had a gut feeling about the semaphore but couldn\u0027t put my finger on it.\n\nGoes to show that semaphores aren\u0027t the ideal abstraction to order thread critical sections sequentially. A `synchronized` monitor lock, or perhaps a `Lock` with a `Condition`, is better for that.\n\nI\u0027d much prefer to have these two semaphores replaced with either of those, to make the sequenced regions explicit. The drawback is that it gets a bit clunky with the loops to deal with \"spurious wakeups\", but it does a much better job at shaking out mistakes like this.\n\nStill marking as optional, because it\u0027s not clear to me how clunky it\u0027d get, and after picking through this I think these two semaphores should be enough (although steps 1 and 2 aren\u0027t technically speaking serialised wrt each other).",
